{"@context":{"@vocab":"https://schema.org/","course":"identifier","wing":"isBasedOn","title":"name","principle":"abstract","skills":"keywords","lessons":"hasPart","key":"identifier","why":"description","statement":"mathExpression","address":"sameAs","skill":"keywords"},"@type":"Course","kind":"school-course","course":"CrossFormulas","wing":"CrossFormulas.lean","title":"Cross Formulas","principle":"THE LEDGER'S OWN ALGEBRA, COUNTED (the captain, 2026-09-25","skills":["cross-formulas"],"level":100,"band":"100–999 steps","rank":122,"lessons":[{"key":"the_arithmetic_alphabet_partitions_by_its_own_algebra","name":"CLAIMED: the 6 arithmetic operators the sealed formulas use split by what they do over the corpus's own integers — 2 commutative (* +), 3 forced on their diagonal (% - /), 1 neither (^) — and 2 + 3 + 1 = 6.","statement":"((2 + 3 + 1 = 6) ∧ (3 > 2)) ∧ (2 > 1)","address":"23ada59a-4cdb-8039-94c3-cdd81827a5c2","skill":"cross-formulas","tex":"2 + 3 + 1 = 6 \\quad\\land\\quad 3 > 2 \\quad\\land\\quad 2 > 1","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></math>","exercise":null},{"key":"most_of_the_unstated_remainder_stays_inside_one_wing","name":"CLAIMED: of 431173 unstated crosses, 89768 join integers no single wing carries all three of — between one 5th and one 4th of them, since 89768 × 4 < 431173 and 89768 × 5 > 431173, so the large majority stays inside a single wing.","statement":"((89768 * 4 < 431173) ∧ (89768 * 5 > 431173)) ∧ (89768 < 431173)","address":"1a824196-122c-8fdc-a77c-d3945c87ebc4","skill":"cross-formulas","tex":"89768 \\cdot 4 < 431173 \\quad\\land\\quad 89768 \\cdot 5 > 431173 \\quad\\land\\quad 89768 < 431173","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>89768</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>431173</mn></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mrow><mn>89768</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>431173</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mn>89768</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>431173</mn></mrow></mrow></math>","exercise":null},{"key":"the_same_arithmetic_answers_more_than_one_domain","name":"CLAIMED: 1524 formula-shaped statements carry 1452 distinct byte-strings and 1319 distinct algebraic forms, so 205 statements restate a form another already holds — and those split 129 copies against 15 crosses, the widest cross spanning 3 wings. Most repetition is waste; a small part of it is a bridge.","statement":"((1319 < 1452) ∧ (1524 - 1319 = 205)) ∧ ((129 > 8 * 15) ∧ (3 > 2))","address":"261e31d9-9339-851c-8a65-bbe7a6f311f4","skill":"cross-formulas","tex":"1319 < 1452 \\quad\\land\\quad 1524 - 1319 = 205 \\quad\\land\\quad 129 > 8 \\cdot 15 \\quad\\land\\quad 3 > 2","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1319</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1452</mn></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mrow><mn>1524</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>1319</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>205</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mrow><mn>129</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></math>","exercise":null},{"key":"the_generated_closure_partitions_into_three_kinds","name":"CLAIMED: of 1953327 crosses the corpus's own integers generate, 1521705 are forced by an operator's algebra, 449 are stated, and 431173 remain — and the three account for the whole, 1521705 + 449 + 431173 = 1953327, with the forced between 3 and 4 times the unstated.","statement":"(1521705 + 449 + 431173 = 1953327) ∧ ((1521705 > 3 * 431173) ∧ (1521705 < 4 * 431173))","address":"02b222e9-f274-8b5c-8a27-f30be0a06ee8","skill":"cross-formulas","tex":"1521705 + 449 + 431173 = 1953327 \\quad\\land\\quad 1521705 > 3 \\cdot 431173 \\quad\\land\\quad 1521705 < 4 \\cdot 431173","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1521705</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>449</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>431173</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1953327</mn></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mrow><mn>1521705</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>431173</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mn>1521705</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>431173</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></math>","exercise":null},{"key":"the_corpus_has_sealed_under_a_hundredth_of_its_own_closure","name":"CLAIMED: the 1524 formula-shaped statements across 113 wings are built from 1279 distinct integers and state 449 crosses, against 431173 their own integers generate unstated — fewer than one in a hundred, since 449 × 100 < 431173, at between 13 and 14 formulas per wing.","statement":"((449 * 100 < 431173) ∧ (1279 > 113)) ∧ ((113 * 13 < 1524) ∧ (113 * 14 > 1524))","address":"ba53bba7-f665-8205-8874-2f095cea49be","skill":"cross-formulas","tex":"449 \\cdot 100 < 431173 \\quad\\land\\quad 1279 > 113 \\quad\\land\\quad 113 \\cdot 13 < 1524 \\quad\\land\\quad 113 \\cdot 14 > 1524","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>449</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>431173</mn></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mn>1279</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>113</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>113</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>13</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1524</mn></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mrow><mn>113</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1524</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></math>","exercise":null}],"exercises":0}
